      "message": "lways returns ``True``. There is no environment lookup, randomness,\n    clock access, or I/O involved, so repeated calls within a process (and\n    across processes) always agree.\n    \"\"\"\n    return True\n```\n\n**Notes:**\n- `feature_flag()` returns the literal `True` unconditionally \u2014 no env vars, randomness, clock, or I/O \u2014 so it is fully deterministic and identical across calls and processes.\n- `CONFIG_NAME = \"E_unrelated_config\"` is a module-level constant.\n- No import of, or call to, `semkg_contract`; any contract-derived semantics are inlined as plain code (only the trivial \"flag is on\" assumption applies here).\n- No other files were created, and no repository-wide tests or unrelated files were touched. The local check sandbox turned out to be isolated from the write sandbox (the file was not visible from `run_command`), so verification was done by re-reading the write result; the code is a two-statement module with no dependencies, so behavior is directly inspectable as shown above."
    },
